# Git and commits

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` sections 10 and 11; details in `rules/git.md`. Apply when committing,
branching, merging or preparing a pull request.

- Check branch and `git status` before editing; stop and ask if the branch is not the agreed one.
- New branches start from a freshly fetched remote default branch.
- Leave the repository on the branch it was found on.
- Never commit, push, force-push, reset, rewrite history or resolve a conflict without being asked.
- One topic per commit. Subject: imperative, about 70 characters, says what changed. Body only for
  why / what was verified / what was left alone. No headings, file lists, emoji or tool mentions.
